    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:accretion_disk_reactor",
      "title": "Accretion Disk Reactor",
      "text": "Feeds matter onto a captive black hole: falling in, it gives up to a third of its rest energy as light. Too much at once, and its own light blows the disk away.$(br2)Generates power.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 3$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Set the hole's mass, how fast it is fed, and its spin. A spinning hole lets matter orbit closer before it falls, so more of its rest energy comes out (6% at no spin, a third near the maximum). The light pushes back on the infalling gas: past the Eddington luminosity, L = 1.26\u00d710\u00b3\u00b9 (M/M\u2609) W, it blows the disk apart."
    },
